  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohammad Sabir Khalid Khan vs The State Of Maharashtra on 20 October, 2022 Author: N.R. Borkar Bench: N.R. Borkar 14-ABA-2638-2022.odt In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2638 Of 2022 Mohammad Sabir Khalid Khan ... Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra ... Respondent ......... Mr. S.K. Ali instructed by A.A. Siddiqui Associate for the Applicant. Ms. P.P. Shinde, App for the State. ......... Coram : N.R. Borkar, J. Dated : 20 October 2022 P.C. :- . This is an application filed under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 for anticipatory bail.",
    "facts": "This is an application filed under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 for anticipatory bail. 2. The applicant is apprehending his arrest in Crime No. 223 of 2022 registered at Taloja Police Station, for the offence punishable under Sections 328, 272, 273, 188 r/w. 34 of Indian Penal Code and Sections 26, 27 and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 3. It appears that tobacco products (gutakha) were seized from the co-accused. The said co-accused during interrogation disclosed the name of the present applicant as supplier of the said tobacco products.",
    "arguments": "5. The learned Counsel for the applicant submits that the issue of applicability of Section 328 of IPC to the tobacco products is still pending before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. It is submitted that nothing is to be recovered at the instance of the present applicant and therefore custodial interrogation of the present applicant is not necessary. 6. On the other hand, the learned APP for the State submits that there are more than five offences of Mohammad Sabir Khalid Khan vs The State Of Maharashtra on 20 October, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/55147816/ 1 similar nature registered against the present applicant. 7.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5. The learned Counsel for the applicant submits that the issue of applicability of Section 328 of IPC to the tobacco products is still pending before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. It is submitted that nothing is to be recovered at the instance of the present applicant and therefore custodial interrogation of the present applicant is not necessary. 6. On the other hand, the learned APP for the State submits that there are more than five offences of Mohammad Sabir Khalid Khan vs The State Of Maharashtra on 20 October, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/55147816/ 1 similar nature registered against the present applicant. 7.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
